-- The previous coordinate proof paired colour indices and needed a separate
-- scalar `skewPairCancels` postulate.  That is unnecessary.  The Langevin
-- connection-energy contribution is already the basis-free bilinear pairing
-- above; at Y=X it vanishes directly by Ad-invariance.  The cancellation is
-- sitewise, and a finite lattice sum remains exactly zero by induction.
--
-- Consequently the compact-Lie connection contributes NO positive symmetric
-- derivative-energy growth constant and NO volume factor.  Once the physical
-- commutator is identified with this geometric ad term, the only nonlocal
